 **Parameters:**
-*   **Step Size ($\Delta x$):** The distance between consecutive samples. Too large causes undersampling (aliasing, missed features); too small causes oversampling (performance loss) [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Threshold ($\alpha_{thresh}$):** The opacity value at which the ray terminates. Commonly 0.99 or 0.95 [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Transfer Function:** Maps scalar values to color and opacity. A simple example provided in [S1, unofficial] uses normalized data range to compute RGB and alpha.
+*   **Step Size ($\Delta x$):** The distance between consecutive samples. Too large causes undersampling (aliasing, missed features); too small causes oversampling (performance loss) [S2, S3, unofficial]. Default is 0.001 [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Threshold ($\alpha_{thresh}$):** The opacity value at which the ray terminates. Commonly 0.95 or 0.99 [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Transfer Function:** Maps scalar values to color and opacity. A simple example provided in [S1, unofficial] uses normalized data range to compute RGB and alpha: $r = (v - DATA_{MIN}) / (DATA_{MAX} - DATA_{MIN})$, $\alpha = 0.9$ if $|r - 0.8| < 0.1$ else $0.01$, R: $(DATA_{MAX} - v) / (DATA_{MAX} - DATA_{MIN})$, G: $1 - |(DATA_{MAX} + DATA_{MIN})/2 - v| \times 2 / (DATA_{MAX} - DATA_{MIN})$, B: $(v - DATA_{MIN}) / (DATA_{MAX} - DATA_{MIN})$ [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Boundary Artifacts:** Incorrect handling of the first and last sample points (entry/exit) can cause stepping artifacts or gaps at the volume boundaries [S3, unofficial]. Strategies must accurately sample corner voxels [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Boundary Artifacts:** Incorrect handling of the first and last sample points (entry/exit) can cause stepping artifacts or gaps at the volume boundaries [S4, unofficial]. Strategies must accurately sample corner voxels to avoid missing corner samples, which causes intensities to drop to zero prematurely when the ray length is shorter than the step size [S4, unofficial].
 *   **Undersampling/Oversampling:** Choosing an inappropriate step size leads to visual artifacts or poor performance [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Missing Corner Samples:** When the ray length is shorter than the step size and corner samples are not explicitly included, intensities drop to zero prematurely [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Gradient Calculation:** Gradients for shading are calculated using a central difference operator with a two-voxel offset rather than a one-voxel offset to avoid normal discontinuities that cause visible rings on smooth surfaces [S1, S3, unofficial].
 
